.TH "WEBTRANSPORT.CREATESENDGROUP" "3JS" "September 1, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
WebTransport.createSendGroup \- WebTransport: createSendGroup() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]createSendGroup()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]WebTransport\f[R] interface creates and returns a
\f[CR]WebTransportSendGroup\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
createSendGroup()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]WebTransportSendGroup\f[R] object.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]InvalidStateError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if the transport\(cqs state is \f[CR]\(dqclosed\(dq\f[R] or
\f[CR]\(dqfailed\(dq\f[R].
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \f[B]\f[CB]createSendGroup()\f[B]\f[R] method creates a new
\f[CR]WebTransportSendGroup\f[R] associated with the
\f[CR]WebTransport\f[R] object on which it is called.
.PP
The \f[CR]WebTransportSendGroup\f[R] object is used to group streams
and/or datagrams created on the same \f[CR]WebTransport\f[R], to control
their relative priority for sending queued bytes.
Within the same group, bytes on higher\-priority streams and datagrams
are sent before bytes from lower\-priority ones.
.PP
The returned \f[CR]WebTransportSendGroup\f[R] is not initially
associated with any streams or datagrams.
You can associate it with a \f[CR]WebTransportDatagramsWritable\f[R] or
\f[CR]WebTransportSendStream\f[R] object in a couple of different ways:
.IP \(bu 2
By passing it as the \f[CR]sendGroup\f[R] option when the object is
created \(em see \f[CR]WebTransport.createUnidirectionalStream()\f[R],
\f[CR]WebTransport.createBidirectionalStream()\f[R], and
\f[CR]WebTransportDatagramDuplexStream.createWritable()\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
By setting the object\(cqs \f[CR]sendGroup\f[R] property afterwards \(em
see \f[CR]WebTransportSendStream.sendGroup\f[R] and
\f[CR]WebTransportDatagramsWritable.sendGroup\f[R].
.PP
Different groups are expected to be treated as equals for the purposes
of bandwidth allocation \(em though the precise way bandwidth is divided
between groups is implementation\-defined.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
This example creates a send group, then associates a unidirectional
stream and the connection\(cqs outgoing datagram stream with it, giving
each a \f[CR]sendOrder\f[R] that defines their relative priority.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] sendGroup = transport.createSendGroup();

\f[B]const\f[R] stream = \f[B]await\f[R] transport.createUnidirectionalStream({
  sendGroup,
  sendOrder: 1,
});

\f[I]// Higher sendOrder: queued bytes on this stream are sent first\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] datagrams = transport.datagrams.createWritable({
  sendGroup,
  sendOrder: 2,
});
.EE
